---
import Profile from "../layouts/Profile.astro";
---

<Profile
  slug="wellness-rd"
  related={["inventor", "business", "quantum-physicist"]}
>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    A health company may know what a device should do long before it knows who
    can make it. As an Associate Scientist at Renatus Wellness, I help translate
    that need into a conversation with manufacturers across India, China and
    Taiwan.
  </Fragment>
  <div slot="lead" class="profile-actions">
    <a
      class="profile-button"
      href="mailto:founder@vishwavigyan.com?subject=Equipment%20development%20enquiry"
    >
      Discuss an equipment idea
    </a>
  </div>
  <aside
    slot="plate"
    class="equipment-note"
    aria-label="Questions for an equipment brief"
  >
    <span class="folio-meta">From the development desk</span>
    <h2>An equipment brief</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>01 / Intended use</dt>
      <dd>Who will use the device, and where?</dd>
      <dt>02 / Design</dt>
      <dd>Is there a drawing, a sample or a working prototype?</dd>
      <dt>03 / Acceptance</dt>
      <dd>What would a sample have to demonstrate?</dd>
    </dl>
  </aside>
  <section class="folio-row">
    <div>
      <span class="stamp">Technology &amp; sourcing</span>
      <h2>Two routes to a sample</h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>
        If a team already has a design, an <strong>OEM</strong> conversation can
        start with its drawings, materials and tolerances. With an{" "}
        <strong>ODM</strong> partner, the manufacturer contributes a design, so
        the first question is which features can be adapted.
      </p>
      <p>
        Consider a handheld unit that will be used for several hours. Its
        weight, grip and power supply are concrete things to discuss when
        comparing samples. A reference photo alone leaves all three open.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="folio-row">
    <h2>Bring the question you have now</h2>
    <div>
      <p>
        If you have a prototype, describe the part that still needs work. If
        you’re sourcing an existing device, describe where it will be used and
        what you need to change. Either is enough to start a conversation.
      </p>
      <p>
        For a public example of how I integrate components from different
        makers,{" "}
        <a href="/inventor/#purakaash">see the Purākaash telescope build</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Profile>
<style>
  .equipment-note {
    border-top: 5px solid var(--leaf);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--leaf) 11%, var(--paper));
    padding: clamp(18px, 3vw, 32px);
  }
  .equipment-note h2 {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .equipment-note dl {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .equipment-note dt {
    padding-top: 0.55rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font: 500 0.71rem var(--mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .equipment-note dd {
    margin: 0.15rem 0 0.7rem;
  }
</style>
